```json
{
  "retryDelay": 5000,
  "apiEndpoint": "https://api.newendpoint.com/v2",
  "otherConfig": "otherValue"
}
```

However, if you are looking to implement this in a TypeScript file that exports a configuration object, here's how you can do it:

FILE: config.ts

```typescript
interface Config {
  retryDelay: number;
  apiEndpoint: string;
  // Add other config properties as needed
}

const config: Config = {
  retryDelay: 5000, // 5 seconds
  apiEndpoint: 'https://api.newendpoint.com/v2',
